{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0133JsjGAL3K8TLtDKFYXQWv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully and propose tasks.\n\n## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It's an experiment in specification-driven development.\n\n**Architecture**: \n- `cmd/<name>/` - one directory per utility\n- `pkg/testutils/` - differential testing framework\n- `pkg/sys/` - syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` - output formatting\n- `pkg/hashutil/` - hash/checksum shared library\n\n\n- `pkg/sizeparse/` - size parsing shared library\n- `pkg/encutil/` - encoding shared library\n- `docs/specs/` - SRDs, use cases, test suites\n- `magefiles/` - build automation\n\n**Current Implementation Status**: Release 00.0 has partial code readiness with `rel00.0-uc003-sys` and `rel00.0-uc006-sizeparse` implemented, while everything else across all releases remains unstarted. All requirements across the SRDs are currently in various states of completion.\n\nLooking at the requirement states more carefully, I notice that `srd002-sys` and `srd087-sizeparse` don't appear in the list at all, which suggests their requirements are already fully implemented. The other SRDs like `srd003-format`, `srd004-ts`, and `srd005-wc` all show \"ready\" status, meaning they have requirements waiting to be addressed.\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is **00.0**, which contains foundational infrastructure. Two items are already done (`sys` and `sizeparse`), but the remaining work includes `magefiles`, `format`, `testutils`, `hashutil`, and `encutil` — all with specs complete but code not yet started.\n\nLooking at the dependencies, `format` relies on `sys` which is finished, while the others have no package dependencies. I'm checking the package contracts to see what each component